nment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:86085fe62ecc11881de1144068e8060dae3c5bc33fc303fecae269f2522854b4","file":"preprints/Deforming-hypersymplectic-four-manifolds-to-hyperkahler-triples-October-7-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":11,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"8a334ae0105f3258eb95032102d7deb54f72440e7fa6954469f766d3df468933","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Deforming-hypersymplectic-four-manifolds-to-hyperkahler-triples-October-7-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:86085fe62ecc11881de1144068e8060dae3c5bc33fc303fecae269f2522854b4","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Deforming-hypersymplectic-four-manifolds-to-hyperkahler-triples-October-7-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L11"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $X$ be a closed connected oriented smooth four-manifold, and let\n$\\omega=(\\omega_1,\\omega_2,\\omega_3)$ be a smooth hypersymplectic structure\nnormalized by\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:intro-normalization}\n \\int_X\\omega_i\\wedge\\omega_j=\\delta_{ij}.\n\\end{equation}\nThere is a smooth family of hypersymplectic structures $\\omega(t)$,\n$0\\le t\\le1$, such that\n\\[\n \\omega(0)=\\omega,\\qquad [\\omega_i(t)]=[\\omega_i]\n \\quad (i=1,2,3),\n\\]\nand a positive volume form $\\mu_1$ with\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:intro-endpoint}\n \\omega_i(1)\\wedge\\omega_j(1)=2\\delta_{ij}\\mu_1.\n\\end{equation}\nThe endpoint forms are parallel and self-dual for a hyperk\\\"ahler metric."}
